# Cline Rules for Pixel Cosmos

## Project overview
- Procedural pixel-art cosmos: cluster → galaxy → star system → body (planet/moon)
- Pure Canvas 2D rendering, no WebGL
- 420×420 px canvas, pixelated image-rendering
- Deterministic universe — everything from a single seed via mulberry32 RNG
- Vite 8 build system, output to docs/

## Rendering
- Planets: bakePlanet() creates offscreen canvas, renderPlanetBody() fills ImageData per frame (lighting, rings, clouds, craters)
- Stars: bakeStar() + renderStar() — granulation, limb darkening, corona rays
- Nebulae: baked once into offscreen canvas
- Orbits, comets, asteroids, ships, selection highlights: pixel fillRect() on main canvas
- Labels: separate #labels canvas overlay with devicePixelRatio scaling
- Overlay canvas (#scene): pointer events for tap/drag/wheel, labels canvas: pointer-events: none

## Scene contract
Each scene must implement a subset of:
- update(dt, t) — physics step
- draw(t) — render to sctx
- drawLabels(t) — render to lctx
- onTap(mx, my), onHover(mx, my), onWheel(mx, my, deltaY)
- onDragStart(), onDragMove(dx, dy, state)
- fit(), zoomBy(f)
- status() → { title, info }
- selectedInfo() → { name, detail }
- primary() → { label, run }
- panelSpec() → array of control descriptors
- search(q) → array of { label, tag, run }

## Ship physics
- Modes: "newton" (patch-conics, manual thrust), "cruise" (FSD superluminal), "landed"
- patched-conics: findPrimary() determines dominant body; state converted at SOI boundary
- fsdTo(target, altitude) — cruise with auto-braking, exits to newton preserving velocity vector
- hohmannTo(sys, targetAlt) — two-impulse transfer between circular orbits
- setManeuverNode(dvProg, dvRad, eta) — timed delta-v node
- circularize(sys) — circularize at current position
- setCircular(sys, selRef, h) — instant circular orbit (used by FSD exit button)

## Key keyboard shortcuts
- 1/2/3/4 — simulation speed presets
- [/] — speed step down/up
- WASD — ship thrust/rotation
- X — kill thrust
- C — circularize orbit
- F — FSD to selected target
- H — Hohmann transfer to selected target
- M — set maneuver node

## File conventions
- No default exports — use named exports only
- JSDoc comments for public functions
- Russian comments/labels for UI text
- Constants extracted at top of files
- RNG order is part of the contract — never reorder rng calls in generators

## Build
- npm run dev — Vite dev server
- npm run build — production build to docs/
- npm run deploy — build + manual git commit (gh-pages)
- .gitignore ignores node_modules, .vite, .env, logs, cache

## Do NOT
- Do NOT introduce WebGL — it was attempted and rolled back due to canvas sync issues
- Do NOT change RNG call order in gen/ files
- Do NOT use default exports
- Do NOT touch docs/ directory manually — it's build output